<article class="env-lemma" id="08LN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08LN">Lemma <span data-tag="08LN">91.5.7</span>.</a> Let $(f, f')$ be a morphism of first order thickenings as in Situation <a href="/tag/08KZ" data-tag="08KZ">91.3.1</a>. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Assume $(f, f')$ is a strict morphism of thickenings and $\mathcal{F}$ flat over $S$. There exists an $\mathcal{O}_{X'}$-module $\mathcal{F}'$ flat over $S'$ with $i^*\mathcal{F}' \cong \mathcal{F}$, if and only if </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the canonical map $ f^*\mathcal{J} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X} \mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{I} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X} \mathcal{F}$ is an isomorphism, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the class $o(\mathcal{F}, \mathcal{I} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X} \mathcal{F}, 1) \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^2_{\mathcal{O}_ X}( \mathcal{F}, \mathcal{I} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X} \mathcal{F})$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/08L8" data-tag="08L8">91.4.4</a> is zero. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from the characterization of $\mathcal{O}_{X'}$-modules flat over $S'$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/08LI" data-tag="08LI">91.5.2</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/08L8" data-tag="08L8">91.4.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>